msgstr "<0/> y <1/> ayudan a reemplazar los enlaces anterior/siguiente:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/upgrade-to-v6.mdx
msgid ""
"<0/> and <1/> now look gray and muted blue. In Ardo 5 both were a saturated "
"blue."
msgstr "<0/> y <1/> son gris y azul apagado en vez del azul saturado de Ardo 5."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"<0/> and <1/> take imported files. Vite gives them fingerprinted URLs, so "
"browsers pick up a new logo after the next deploy instead of serving a cached "
"one. Here the logo doubles as the favicon; pass a square mark to <2/> when "
"your logo is a wordmark."
msgstr ""
"<0/> e <1/> reciben archivos importados. Vite añade huellas a las URL para "
"renovar la caché al desplegar. Aquí el logotipo sirve de favicon; para una "
"marca textual, pasa una imagen cuadrada a <2/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid "<0/> and the config types."
msgstr "<0/> y tipos de configuración."

#: docs/app/content/guide/layout-and-navigation.mdx
msgid ""
"<0/> can export <1/>. For a missing page, Ardo renders it inside the root, so "
"the header and sidebar stay. For a render error, it replaces the root, so "
"broken chrome cannot hide the error. Without the export, Ardo uses <2/> from "
"<3/>."
msgstr ""
"<0/> puede exportar <1/>. Una página ausente aparece dentro de la raíz con "
"navegación; un error de render reemplaza la raíz para seguir visible. Sin "
"export, Ardo usa <2/> de <3/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/layout-and-navigation.mdx
msgid ""
"<0/> can own its open state when <1/> is omitted. Its <2/>, <3/>, <4/>, <5/>, "
"and <6/> props customize the panel; <7/>, <8/> (button content), and <9/> "
"customize the trigger. The trigger follows Ardo's 1024px mobile breakpoint. "
"Use controlled state, as above, to close navigation before activating search. "
"Both dialogs handle Escape and restore focus. <10/> accepts <11/> for the "
"standard responsive field or <12/> for an icon at every width."
msgstr ""
"Sin <1/>, <0/> gestiona su estado. <2/>, <3/>, <4/>, <5/> y <6/> ajustan el "
"panel; <7/>, <8/> y <9/> ajustan el botón visible bajo 1024 px. El estado "
"controlado permite cerrar el menú antes de buscar. Escape cierra los "
"diálogos y restaura el foco. <10/> acepta <11/> o <12/>."

