"<1/> y <2/> de <3/>. Tonos, <4/> y tokens van en <6/> de <5/>; logotipos y "
"favicons son imports con huellas de Vite. Un <7/> antiguo produce un error con"
" enlace a esta guía."

#: docs/app/content/guide/frontmatter.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo also renders <0/> as the visible lede under the page title. If the first "
"body paragraph has the same normalized text, Ardo skips the lede to avoid "
"showing the sentence twice."
msgstr ""
"Ardo también muestra <0/> como introducción bajo el título. Si el primer "
"párrafo tiene el mismo texto normalizado, omite la introducción para evitar "
"repetir la frase."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo brings that simple static-docs shape to React. If your app, examples, and"
" design system are React, Ardo lets you reuse them instead of rewriting them "
"in Vue."
msgstr ""
"Ardo lleva esa sencillez a React. Si la aplicación, ejemplos y sistema de "
"diseño usan React, reutilízalos en lugar de reescribirlos en Vue."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo builds every locale as an explicit static route tree and renders a locale"
" switcher when more than one locale is configured. Put the translated "
"documents in <0/>; for example, <1/> and <2/>."
msgstr ""
"Ardo construye cada idioma como un árbol estático y muestra un selector si "
"hay varios configurados. Coloca las traducciones en <0/>, por ejemplo <1/> y "
"<2/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo bundles the application's dependencies for SSR, including its React "
"runtime. Components and the server renderer use that same bundled runtime. "
"There is no per-component <0/> list to maintain. A missing dependency produces"
" an <1/> error rather than falling back to a parent installation. During "
"development, Vite automatically optimizes SSR dependencies so CommonJS "
"libraries can run in the same module graph."
msgstr ""
"Ardo empaqueta las dependencias SSR con React. Los componentes y el renderer "
"comparten esa ejecución; no hace falta una lista <0/> por componente. Una "
"dependencia ausente produce un error <1/>, sin recurrir a instalaciones "
"superiores. Vite optimiza las dependencias SSR en desarrollo para que CommonJS"
" funcione en el mismo grafo."

#: docs/app/content/guide/api-documentation.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo can turn a local OpenAPI 3.0 or 3.1 specification into static MDX "
"reference pages. The generated pages use the ordinary route, sidebar, search, "
"sitemap, link-check, and LLM-output pipeline, so an API reference behaves like"
" the rest of the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Ardo convierte una especificación OpenAPI 3.0 o 3.1 local en páginas MDX "
"estáticas. Usan las mismas rutas, barras laterales, búsqueda, sitemap, "
"comprobaciones y exportaciones LLM que el resto del sitio."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo clears both output directories by default. Use <0/> to retain existing "
"files. An explicit <1/> in <2/> sets the same policy; an environment's <3/> or"
" <4/> takes precedence."
msgstr ""
"Ardo vacía ambos directorios por defecto. <0/> conserva los archivos. <1/> en"
" <2/> aplica la misma regla; los ajustes de <3/> o <4/> tienen prioridad."

#: docs/app/content/guide/frontmatter.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo combines page-level redirects with the <0><1/></0> option in <2/> and "
"emits host-friendly redirect assets during production builds."
msgstr ""
"Ardo combina estas redirecciones con <0><1/></0> de <2/> y genera los archivos"
" adecuados para los proveedores en la compilación de producción."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo generates a lean favicon set from its owl at build time and serves it "
"during development: <0/>, <1/>, and <2/>. Your own icon is an imported file on"
" <3/>, <4/>, so Vite fingerprints it; see <5>Theming</5>. A file of the same "
"name in <6/> replaces the generated one, and <7/> leaves all three to you."
msgstr ""
"Ardo genera los iconos de búho <0/>, <1/> y <2/> durante el build y los sirve"
" en desarrollo. Importa tu icono con <3/>, <4/>, para que Vite añada su "
"huella; consulta <5>Temas</5>. Un archivo homónimo en <6/> reemplaza el "
"generado. <7/> te deja gestionar los tres."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo generates its route table as a virtual module; there are no generated "
"router types to rebuild. Check the authored route and its imports:"
msgstr ""
"La tabla de rutas es virtual; no hay tipos del router que regenerar. Comprueba"
" la ruta y sus imports:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo handles the framework UI with Vanilla Extract. Tailwind is for "
"<0>your</0> content, so you can style without leaving React or adding a second"
" theme system."
msgstr ""
"Ardo usa Vanilla Extract para su interfaz. Tailwind sirve a <0>tus</0> "
"contenidos: estilos en React sin otro sistema de temas."

#: docs/app/content/guide/components.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo includes 50 <0>Streamline Core Line</0> icons for documentation content. "
"They share the same 14 × 14 grid, rounded strokes, and <1/> as the built-in "
"sidebar and header controls."
msgstr ""
"Ardo incluye 50 iconos <0>Streamline Core Line</0>. Comparten la cuadrícula "
"14×14, trazos redondeados y <1/> de los controles de navegación."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is built on Vite and Rust-based Markdown and highlighting engines instead"
" of webpack-era architecture, and it prerenders every page to static HTML "
"without a client-side router. It has a smaller configuration surface and a "
"more codebase-native model for teams already using modern React tooling."
msgstr ""
"Ardo usa Vite y motores Rust para Markdown y resaltado en lugar de una "
"arquitectura Webpack. Prerenderiza sin router del cliente y ofrece menos "
"configuración para equipos React modernos."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is for React teams that want modern static docs without leaving React or "
"moving their docs into a closed platform. That makes the comparison more "
"specific than \"which docs tool is best?\" Docusaurus, Starlight, VitePress, "
"Nextra, Fumadocs, and Mintlify are all strong tools. The better question is: "
"<0>where should your docs live, and how much of your existing React code "
"should they reuse?</0>"
msgstr ""
"Ardo se dirige a equipos React que quieren documentación estática moderna en"
" su repositorio. Docusaurus, Starlight, VitePress, Nextra, Fumadocs y Mintlify"
" son buenas herramientas. La pregunta es: <0>¿dónde debe vivir tu "
"documentación y cuánto código React debe reutilizar?</0>"

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is intentionally narrower. It gives you a complete static docs product "
"around React, Vite, MDX, and native API documentation, with fewer "
"architectural choices to make."
msgstr ""
"Ardo es deliberadamente más acotado: un producto estático completo con "
"React, Vite, MDX y API nativa, con menos decisiones de arquitectura."

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/index.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is intentionally not trying to become every kind of documentation "
"product."
msgstr "Ardo se centra en un enfoque concreto de la documentación."

#: docs/app/content/guide/markdown.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is Markdown-first, but it does not trap you in Markdown. Start with plain"
" prose and code blocks; when a page needs a live React example, a custom "
"component, or a design-system callout, switch to MDX without changing tools."
msgstr ""
"Ardo empieza con Markdown sin limitarte a él. Usa texto y bloques de código;"
" pasa a MDX cuando necesites un ejemplo React interactivo, un componente o un "
"aviso del sistema de diseño, sin cambiar de herramientas."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is not tied to Next.js. It is a Vite-based React docs stack that writes "
"one static HTML page per route, with no client-side router. That makes it a "
"better fit when your React app is not a Next app, or when you want "
"documentation as a smaller, focused static build."
msgstr ""
"Ardo no depende de Next.js. Su build Vite/React escribe HTML estático por "
"ruta, sin router del cliente. Encaja fuera de Next o para una documentación "
"estática independiente y acotada."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is open source and codebase-native. Your docs live in your repository, "
"build in your CI, deploy as static files, and render with your React "
"components."
msgstr ""
"Ardo es de código abierto y vive en tu repositorio: compilación en CI, "
"archivos estáticos y renderizado con tus componentes React."

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/index.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is repository-native and self-hosted. Teams that want hosted "
"collaboration should use a hosted docs platform."
msgstr ""
"Ardo sigue ligado al repositorio y autoalojado. Elige una plataforma alojada "
"para esa colaboración."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo is strongest when documentation should live next to a React codebase:"
msgstr "Ardo encaja especialmente junto a una base de código React:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo keeps browser-safe runtime imports separate from build-time Node.js "
"imports:"
msgstr ""
"Ardo separa los imports para navegador de los imports del build de Node.js:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo loads <0/> for every site, after the CSS your root module imports. It "
"includes the complete UI, reset, and theme styles in the named <1/> cascade "
"layer. Component imports do not load another copy of the stylesheet, and "
"neither does importing it yourself."
msgstr ""
"Ardo carga <0/> después de los imports CSS de la raíz. Contiene interfaz, "
"reset y tema en la capa <1/>. Los imports de componentes o uno explícito no "
"añaden una segunda copia."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo loads its own stylesheet for every site. If your own styles don't apply, "
"check that <0/> imports your CSS file, and see <1>Stylesheet ownership and "
"cascade</1> for how Ardo's <2/> cascade layer interacts with yours."
msgstr ""
"Ardo carga sus estilos automáticamente. Comprueba el import CSS de <0/> y la "
"<1>cascada</1> para entender su interacción con la capa <2/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo manages document format, YAML frontmatter, React component bindings, and "
"removal of a matching first page-title heading. The former remark, rehype, and"
" recma plugin options have been removed; see <0>Upgrade to Ardo 5</0>."
msgstr ""
"Ardo gestiona el formato, el frontmatter YAML, los componentes React y la "
"eliminación del primer título si coincide con el de página. Se eliminaron "
"las opciones remark, rehype y recma; consulta <0>Actualizar a Ardo 5</0>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/getting-started.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo manages React, React DOM, and Vite as its own dependencies. Its CLI "
"starts the development server, builds the static site, and previews the "
"generated client output:"
msgstr ""
"Ardo gestiona React, React DOM y Vite como dependencias propias. Su CLI "
"arranca el servidor de desarrollo, compila el sitio estático y permite "
"previsualizar la salida del cliente:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/frontmatter.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo normalizes documented frontmatter once for route metadata, sidebars, "
"search, redirects, sitemap, and LLM output. Invalid values are reported with "
"the source file during production builds. Unknown fields remain compatible by "
"default, but can be made visible or blocking in <0>Configuration</0>."
msgstr ""
"Ardo normaliza los campos documentados una sola vez para metadatos, barras "
"laterales, búsqueda, redirecciones, sitemap y exportaciones LLM. La "
"compilación de producción indica los valores no válidos y su archivo. Los "
"campos desconocidos se aceptan por defecto, pero puedes señalarlos o "
"bloquearlos en la <0>configuración</0>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo owns the React, React DOM, Vite, and default icon installations. Imports "
"of these managed packages resolve to Ardo's dependency tree. Other direct "
"application imports must be declared in the docs package, even when another "
"dependency already uses that package. Dependencies may use their own declared "
"transitive dependencies. Normal pnpm links to packages in its virtual store "
"are supported; the store location does not change package ownership."
msgstr ""
"Ardo gestiona React, React DOM, Vite e iconos predeterminados desde su árbol "
"de dependencias. Los demás imports directos deben declararse en el paquete de"
" documentación, aunque otra dependencia ya los use. Las dependencias pueden "
"usar sus paquetes transitivos declarados. Se admiten los enlaces pnpm normales"
" al almacén virtual; su ubicación no cambia la pertenencia del paquete."

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/index.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo prioritizes React-native reuse. Astro, VitePress, or Starlight can be "
"better for prose-only sites."
msgstr ""
"Prima la reutilización de React. Astro, VitePress o Starlight pueden servir "
"mejor para texto puro."

#: docs/app/content/guide/deployment.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo produces a fully static site out of the box. Your docs can stay in your "
"repository, build in your CI pipeline, and deploy to any provider that serves "
"files. When you run <0/>, Ardo prerenders every page to static HTML, so no "
"server is needed at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Ardo genera un sitio completamente estático. La documentación puede vivir en"
" el repositorio, compilarse en CI y publicarse en cualquier proveedor que "
"sirva archivos. <0/> prerenderiza todas las páginas como HTML estático: no "
"hace falta servidor en ejecución."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo provides its own base styles for documentation content — typography, "
"headings, links, lists, and code blocks. Tailwind's Preflight reset would "
"conflict with these styles and break the default look."
msgstr ""
"Ardo aporta estilos base de tipografía, títulos, enlaces, listas y código. "
"El reset Preflight entraría en conflicto con esa apariencia."

#: docs/app/content/guide/api-documentation.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo reads your declarations through the native API of TypeScript 7.1, which "
"also typechecks your project. TypeScript 7.0 does not work: its native API is "
"still marked unstable and lacks the snapshot, emit and module resolution calls"
" Ardo uses. The supported build is a pinned nightly; it is not a released 7.1 "
"beta. Projects that installed it as the <0/> alias keep working."
msgstr ""
"Ardo lee las declaraciones con la API nativa de TypeScript 7.1, que también "
"comprueba los tipos. TypeScript 7.0 no sirve: su API inestable carece de las "
"llamadas de snapshot, emisión y resolución necesarias. Se admite una nightly"
" fijada, no una beta 7.1 publicada. Los proyectos que usan el alias <0/> "
"siguen funcionando."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo releases the framework, UI, and runtime as one package. Setup uses "
"<0>versioned Agent Instructions</0> and the tested Basic example. See the "
"<1>Ardo changelog</1> for release history."
msgstr ""
"Framework, interfaz y runtime se publican juntos. La instalación sigue las "
"<0>instrucciones versionadas</0> y Basic probado. Consulta el "
"<1>historial</1>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/index.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo releases the framework, UI, and runtime as one package. This page keeps "
"product claims grounded: what is ready to use today, what still evolves, and "
"what is planned. The <0>changelog</0> lists every release."
msgstr ""
"Ardo publica framework, interfaz y ejecución en un único paquete. Esta "
"página distingue funciones disponibles, experimentales y previstas. El "
"<0>registro de cambios</0> detalla cada versión."

#: docs/app/content/guide/layout-and-navigation.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo renders every page inside an HTML shell: <0/>, <1/>, and <2/>. The shell "
"is rendered on the server only, during <3/> and <4/>; the root component "
"inside it hydrates. By default, Ardo uses <5/> from <6/>. It adds the charset "
"and viewport tags, the theme bootstrap script, favicons, the page's title and "
"meta tags, stylesheets, and the client script. Most sites do not need a <7/> "
"export."
msgstr ""
"Ardo renderiza cada página en un shell HTML: <0/>, <1/> y <2/>. Solo se "
"renderiza en el servidor durante <3/> y <4/>; la raíz interior se hidrata. "
"Por defecto, <5/> de <6/> añade codificación, viewport, script de tema, "
"favicons, título, metadatos, estilos y script cliente. Rara vez necesitas un "
"export <7/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo requires Node.js 22.22 or newer and native binaries for Linux or Windows "
"on x64/arm64, or macOS on Apple Silicon. Keep optional dependencies enabled "
"when installing packages."
msgstr ""
"Ardo necesita Node.js 22.22 o posterior y binarios Linux/Windows x64/arm64 o "
"macOS Apple Silicon. Activa las dependencias opcionales al instalar."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid "Ardo requires Node.js 22.22.0 or higher. Check your version:"
msgstr "Ardo necesita Node.js 22.22.0 o posterior. Comprueba tu versión:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/components.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo ships the components documentation pages need most: callouts, badges, "
"cards, tabs, accordions, steps, code blocks, icons, and landing-page blocks. "
"Each one follows the theme in light and dark mode and works with the keyboard."
" The examples below run in the real layout of this site, so switch the theme "
"in the header or resize the window to see them in context."
msgstr ""
"Ardo incluye avisos, insignias, tarjetas, pestañas, acordeones, pasos, "
"bloques de código, iconos y elementos de portada. Siguen los temas claro y "
"oscuro y funcionan con teclado. Los ejemplos usan el diseño real: cambia el "
"tema o el tamaño de ventana para comprobarlos."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo ships with a complete theme so you can focus on content, not design:"
msgstr "Ardo incluye un tema completo para que te centres en el contenido:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/markdown.mdx
msgid "Ardo supports GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM) out of the box."
msgstr "Ardo admite GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM) de serie."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo takes a different approach. Instead of inventing a new system, it builds "
"on what the React ecosystem already provides."
msgstr "Ardo se apoya en las posibilidades que React ya ofrece."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo targets modern evergreen browsers supported by React 19 and Vite 8. The "
"default theme uses modern CSS such as OKLCH color and custom properties; teams"
" with legacy browser requirements should test their final docs build against "
"their own support matrix."
msgstr ""
"Ardo se dirige a navegadores modernos compatibles con React 19 y Vite 8. El "
"tema usa OKLCH y propiedades CSS personalizadas. Prueba el build final con tu "
"matriz si necesitas navegadores antiguos."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo treats React as the native component model. You can use React providers, "
"hooks, and interactive examples in MDX, including an installed design-system "
"package. In Starlight, React runs through Astro islands, which is powerful but"
" creates a different boundary."
msgstr ""
"React es el modelo nativo de Ardo: proveedores, hooks y ejemplos MDX "
"interactivos funcionan también con sistemas de diseño instalados. Starlight "
"usa islas Astro, potentes pero con otro límite."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo treats the Vite project root as an independent documentation package. "
"Keep its own <0/> and install its declared dependencies in that project's "
"<1/>. An installation in an ancestor or monorepo root does not satisfy a "
"missing local installation."
msgstr ""
"Ardo trata la raíz Vite como un paquete independiente. Mantén allí una <0/>"
" e instala sus dependencias en su propio <1/>. Una instalación en un "
"directorio padre o la raíz del monorepositorio no sustituye una instalación "
"local ausente."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo uses page frontmatter titles and descriptions when available, skips TSX "
"routes, and strips MDX imports, exports, and JSX component tags from the full "
"export. Set <0/> in page frontmatter to exclude a Markdown page from both "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Ardo usa los títulos y descripciones del frontmatter, omite las rutas TSX y "
"elimina imports, exports y etiquetas JSX del texto completo. <0/> en el "
"frontmatter excluye una página Markdown de ambos archivos."

#: docs/app/content/guide/markdown.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo uses standard MDX modules, so reusable content snippets work without a "
"custom syntax or plugin. Put shared fragments in a <0/> directory and import "
"them wherever you need the same content."
msgstr ""
"Ardo usa módulos MDX estándar: reutilizar contenido no necesita sintaxis ni "
"plugins especiales. Pon los fragmentos en <0/> e impórtalos donde hagan "
"falta."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo validates its documented frontmatter fields once while it scans route "
"metadata. Diagnostics name the source file and never feed malformed values "
"into sidebar, search, sitemap, redirect, or LLM output. Turn strict mode on "
"when a project wants misspelled metadata to fail CI:"
msgstr ""
"Ardo valida los campos documentados del frontmatter al recorrer las rutas. Los"
" diagnósticos citan el archivo; los valores inválidos no llegan a la "
"navegación, búsqueda, sitemap, redirecciones o salidas LLM. Activa el modo "
"estricto para que los errores hagan fallar la CI:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/getting-started.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo works without a configuration file. Add <0/> for site metadata, "
"deployment, or content options. UI configuration, including the theme, "
"navigation, sidebar, and footer, stays in JSX props in <1/>:"
msgstr ""
"Ardo funciona sin archivo de configuración. Añade <0/> para metadatos, "
"despliegue o contenido. El tema, la navegación, la barra lateral y el pie de "
"página se configuran mediante props JSX en <1/>:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/content-sources.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo writes mapped files under the selected <0/> directory and marks it as "
"generated. Edit the original source, never the materialized route. The plugin "
"refuses to delete a non-empty handwritten target directory, so use a dedicated"
" prefix such as <1/>."
msgstr ""
"Ardo escribe los archivos asociados en el directorio <0/> elegido y lo marca "
"como generado. Edita la fuente original, nunca la ruta generada. El plugin no "
"elimina directorios de destino escritos a mano que contengan archivos. Usa un "
"prefijo específico, como <1/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo writes one HTML file per page and uses ordinary document navigation. "
"Deploy the complete <0/> directory and configure the host to serve directory "
"indexes, such as <1/> for <2/>. Preserve the configured base path and serve "
"Ardo's <3/> for missing pages. See <4>Deployment</4> for host-specific "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"Ardo escribe un HTML por página y usa navegación normal entre documentos. "
"Publica todo <0/> y sirve los índices de directorio, como <1/> para <2/>. "
"Conserva la ruta base y usa <3/> para páginas ausentes. Consulta "
"<4>Despliegue</4>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo writes the generated files below <0/> and marks the directory with <1/>. "
"It refuses to replace a non-empty target directory without that marker. When a"
" source file has no frontmatter, Ardo synthesizes <2/> from the first <3/> "
"heading or filename and <4/> from a numeric filename prefix such as <5/>."
msgstr ""
"Ardo escribe bajo <0/> y añade <1/>. No reemplaza un directorio no vacío sin"
" ese marcador. Sin frontmatter, deriva <2/> del primer título <3/> o del "
"archivo y <4/> de un prefijo numérico como <5/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/components.mdx
msgid "ardo.config.ts"
msgstr "ardo.config.ts"

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/upgrade-to-v6.mdx
msgid "Ardo's built-in client entry, which hydrates every page."
msgstr "Entrada cliente integrada para hidratar las páginas."

#: docs/app/content/guide/releases/upgrade-to-v6.mdx
msgid "Ardo's built-in server renderer. <0/> no longer exists."
msgstr "Render servidor integrado; desaparece <0/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/troubleshooting.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's CLI adds its build integration automatically. Put site settings in "
"optional <0/>:"
msgstr ""
"La CLI añade la integración automáticamente. Pon los ajustes del sitio en "
"el archivo opcional <0/>:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's CLI reads optional site configuration from <0/>. Most sites do not need"
" a Vite configuration file: <1/>, <2/>, and <3/> provide the framework "
"integration. Keep UI behavior in React: <4/>, header/sidebar/footer props, "
"component overrides, and runtime hooks."
msgstr ""
"La CLI lee la configuración opcional de <0/>. La mayoría de sitios no "
"necesita una configuración de Vite: <1/>, <2/> y <3/> proporcionan la "
"integración. Configura la interfaz en React mediante <4/>, las props de "
"cabecera, barra lateral y pie, los componentes y los hooks de ejecución."

#: docs/app/content/guide/markdown.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's components work in MDX without imports: callouts, badges, cards, tabs, "
"accordions, steps, code blocks, and icons. <0>Components</0> shows each one "
"live, with its MDX and its props."
msgstr ""
"Los componentes Ardo funcionan sin imports en MDX: avisos, badges, tarjetas, "
"pestañas, acordeones, pasos, bloques e iconos. <0>Componentes</0> los muestra"
" con su MDX y props."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's config file holds no colors or assets. It covers what the build needs: "
"title, base path, versions, and the API reference."
msgstr ""
"La configuración no contiene colores ni recursos, sino datos del build: "
"título, base, versiones y referencia API."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's content styles set list markers, table borders, code styles, and "
"spacing explicitly, so Markdown content stays readable even when a host reset "
"clears browser defaults. Because the <0/> layer sits after <1/>, Preflight "
"cannot undo Ardo's styles, and because it sits before <2/>, your utility "
"classes still win where you apply them."
msgstr ""
"Ardo define explícitamente marcadores, bordes de tablas, código y espacios. "
"El contenido sigue legible con un reset del host. <0/> va después de <1/>, "
"por lo que Preflight no lo anula, y antes de <2/>, que conserva la prioridad."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's default theme is complete, and you change it where you build the rest "
"of the site: in <0/>, with React props and imported files. Start with a few "
"hues and go deeper when you need to:"
msgstr ""
"El tema Ardo está completo. Personalízalo donde compones el sitio: en <0/>, "
"con props React y archivos importados. Empieza por unos tonos:"

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo's generated Vanilla Extract class names are implementation details. Use "
"the stable hook classes for narrowly scoped overrides:"
msgstr ""
"Las clases generadas son internas. Usa las clases estables para ajustes "
"concretos:"

