#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Every component in Ardo is a React component. Your documentation layout, "
"custom callouts, and interactive examples use standard React. Keep authored "
"components inside the docs project, or install a packaged component library "
"there and import its public exports. Use the hooks you already know and write "
"TypeScript."
msgstr ""
"Cada componente Ardo es React. Diseños, avisos y ejemplos interactivos usan "
"React normal. Guarda tus componentes en el proyecto o instala una biblioteca e"
" importa sus exports públicos. Usa los hooks que conoces y TypeScript."

#: docs/app/content/guide/what-is-ardo.mdx
msgid ""
"Every file in <0/> becomes a page, and every page is prerendered to its own "
"HTML file. Links are ordinary links, so pages load fast from any static host, "
"and the parts that need React hydrate in the browser. There is no client "
"router to configure, and the build checks that every internal link points to a"
" page that exists."
msgstr ""
"Cada archivo de <0/> genera una página HTML prerenderizada. Los enlaces "
"normales cargan rápido desde cualquier alojamiento estático y las partes "
"interactivas se hidratan en el navegador. No hay router del cliente que "
"configurar; la compilación comprueba los destinos internos."

#: docs/app/content/guide/theming.mdx
msgid ""
"Every token is also a CSS variable, such as <0/> or <1/>, so a plain "
"stylesheet can set them too. Ardo ships its defaults in the <2/> cascade "
"layer, and your unlayered CSS beats them. A color set on <3/> therefore "
"applies in dark mode as well; scope colors to one scheme:"
msgstr ""
"Cada token es también una variable CSS, como <0/> o <1/>. Tus estilos sin "
"capa prevalecen sobre la capa <2/>. Un color en <3/> también se aplica en "
"oscuro; limita los colores a su modo:"

