#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"When <0/> is set, Ardo treats it as the deployment root and appends the "
"version path. For example, <1/> with <2/> produces canonical URLs under <3/>. "
"The generated sitemap contains the current build only; older major versions "
"can remain deployed as static folders without being advertised as duplicate "
"current content."
msgstr ""
"Ardo añade la ruta de versión a <0/>: <1/> y <2/> producen <3/>. El sitemap "
"solo incluye el build actual. Las versiones antiguas pueden permanecer en "
"carpetas estáticas sin anunciarse como contenido actual duplicado."

#: docs/app/content/guide/deployment.mdx
msgid ""
"When <0/> lists older major versions, do not upload only the fresh <1/> folder"
" to GitHub Pages. GitHub Pages replaces the full artifact on every deploy, so "
"use a staging directory that combines the current build with retained static "
"folders for older majors before calling <2/>."
msgstr ""
"Si <0/> incluye versiones anteriores, no subas únicamente el nuevo <1/>. "
"GitHub Pages sustituye todo el artefacto en cada despliegue. Antes de <2/>, "
"combina el build actual y las carpetas antiguas conservadas en un directorio "
"de preparación."

#: docs/app/content/guide/configuration.mdx
msgid ""
"When <0/> points to a single file, Ardo writes it as <1/> or <2/>, so <3/> "
"becomes the <4/> route."
msgstr ""
"Cuando <0/> apunta a un solo archivo, Ardo lo escribe como <1/> o <2/>. Así, "
"<3/> se convierte en la ruta <4/>."

#: docs/app/content/guide/frontmatter.mdx
msgid ""
"When a route directory contains <0/> or <1/>, its frontmatter configures the "
"generated directory group rendered by <2/>."
msgstr ""
"Si un directorio de rutas contiene <0/> o <1/>, su frontmatter configura el "
"grupo generado por <2/>."

